<title>CANADA: Canada welcomes NATO-Russia agreement.</title>
<headline>Canada welcomes NATO-Russia agreement.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian Foreign Minister Lloyd Axworthy on Thursday welcomed the successful conclusion of negotiations on a new framework for NATO-Russia relations.</p>
<p>&quot;The new NATO-Russia relationship marks an important stage in the evolution of the post-Cold War European security structure,&quot; Axworthy said in a statement.</p>
<p>NATO and Russia, former Cold War foes, said on Wednesday they had reached agreement to create a new partnership. It came as NATO prepares, in the face of Russian opposition, to admit new members from the former Soviet bloc.</p>
</text>
